#: src/reference/lints.md:403
msgid "`text_direction_codepoint_in_comment`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:404 src/reference/lints.md:425
msgid "Group: `correctness`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:406 src/reference/lints.md:427
msgid "Level: `deny`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:411
msgid ""
"Detects Unicode codepoints in manifest comments that change the visual "
"representation of text on screen in a way that does not correspond to their "
"on memory representation."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:415
msgid ""
"Unicode allows changing the visual flow of text on screen in order to "
"support scripts that are written right-to-left, but a specially crafted "
"comment can make code that will be compiled appear to be part of a comment, "
"depending on the software used to read the code. To avoid potential problems "
"or confusion, such as in CVE-2021-42574, by default we deny their use."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:424
msgid "`text_direction_codepoint_in_literal`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:432
msgid ""
"Detects Unicode codepoints in literals in manifests that change the visual "
"representation of text on screen in a way that does not correspond to their "
"on memory representation."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:436
msgid ""
"Unicode allows changing the visual flow of text on screen in order to "
"support scripts that are written right-to-left, but a specially crafted "
"literal can make code that will be compiled appear to be part of a literal, "
"depending on the software used to read the code. To avoid potential problems "
"or confusion, such as in CVE-2021-42574, by default we deny their use."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:445
msgid "`unknown_lints`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:453
msgid "Checks for unknown lints in the `[lints.cargo]` table"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:456
msgid ""
"The lint name could be misspelled, leading to confusion as to why it is not "
"working as expected"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:458
msgid ""
"The unknown lint could end up causing an error if `cargo` decides to make a "
"lint with the same name in the future"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:462
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[lints.cargo]\n"
"this-lint-does-not-exist = \"warn\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:468
msgid "`unused_dependencies`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:477
msgid "Checks for dependencies that are not used by any of the cargo targets."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:481
msgid "Slows down compilation time."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:485
msgid ""
"The lint is only emitted in specific circumstances as multiple cargo targets "
"exist for the different dependencies tables and they must all be built to "
"know if a dependency is unused. Currently, only the selected packages are "
"checked and not all `path` dependencies like most lints. The cargo target "
"selection flags, independent of which packages are selected, determine which "
"dependencies tables are checked. As there is no way to select all cargo "
"targets that use `[dev-dependencies]`, they are unchecked."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:493
msgid "Examples:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:494
msgid "`cargo check` will lint `[build-dependencies]` and `[dependencies]`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:495
msgid ""
"`cargo check --all-targets` will still only lint `[build-dependencies]` and "
"`[dependencies]` and not `[dev-dependencoes]`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:496
msgid ""
"`cargo check --bin foo` will not lint `[dependencies]` even if `foo` is the "
"only bin though `[build-dependencies]` will be checked"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:497
msgid ""
"`cargo check -p foo` will not lint any dependencies tables for the `path` "
"dependency `bar` even if `bar` only has a `[lib]`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:499
msgid ""
"There can be false positives when depending on a transitive dependency to "
"activate a feature."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:501
msgid ""
"For false positives from pinning the version of a transitive dependency in "
"`Cargo.toml`, move the dependency to the `target.\"cfg(false)\"."
"dependencies` table."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:506
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[package]\n"
"name = \"foo\"\n"
"\n"
"[dependencies]\n"
"unused = \"1\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:522
msgid "`unused_workspace_dependencies`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:530
msgid ""
"Checks for any entry in `[workspace.dependencies]` that has not been "
"inherited"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:533
msgid "They can give the false impression that these dependencies are used"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:536
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[workspace.dependencies]\n"
"regex = \"1\"\n"
"\n"
"[dependencies]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:544
msgid "`unused_workspace_package_fields`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:552
msgid ""
"Checks for any fields in `[workspace.package]` that has not been inherited"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:555
msgid "They can give the false impression that these fields are used"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/lints.md:558
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[workspace.package]\n"
"edition = \"2024\"\n"
"\n"
"[package]\n"
"name = \"foo\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
